        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harvey Pekar, Denise Levertov, Joyce Brabner\n- Works: American Splendor, A Door in the Hive, August Houseplant\n- Roles: comic book writer, music critic, media personality, poet, political comics writer\n\nFacts:\n- Denise Levertov, born Priscilla Denise Levertov, was an American poet who lived from October 24, 1923 to December 20, 1997.\n- Harvey Pekar was an American underground comic book writer, music critic, and media personality who lived from October 8, 1939 to July 12, 2010.\n- Joyce Brabner, born March 1, 1952, is a writer of political comics and the widow of Harvey Pekar.\n- Harvey Pekar was best known for the autobiographical comic series American Splendor.\n- Denise Levertov wrote the collection A Door in the Hive.\n- August Houseplant is a poem from Denise Levertov's collection A Door in the Hive.",
